  "notes": "Dusty-rose pigmented-render bar along the plot, street (north) side nearly blind, garden (south) side opening under a timber gallery. From the street elevation (two long wall segments split by a narrow entry with a lattice gate, a perforated-block screen, small projecting lamp boxes), the driveway and carport views (the north wall level; the east volume's top rising to a sharp peak at its south-east corner, falling west along the south face and north across the east end; the carport cut into the east end under it; a lower wall plane standing in front of the north face), the garden views (continuous timber-post gallery with a slatted roof and deck, sliding glass behind it, a chimney flue), the detached black-framed glass pavilion with vertical screens and a grey fascia, and the long linear pool with rose coping parallel to the gallery, a big tree at its west end. This pass: the render is 'rose' (it was 'brick'), the pool coping too; the feather grass is 'drygrass' tufts in drifts along the gallery, the pool and the beds (it was 'thatch' mounds); the prow is rebuilt as two falls from the south-east peak (strips of sheds, each rising east and capped by the fall to the north), where before it rose one way only; the east bar is taller (4.6 m) than the west (4.0 m) as the garden view shows; the carport opens in the east end instead of the north face, with a timber back wall and a post at the corner; a gravel apron before it. Guessed: overall length (~50 m, from the gate and a door), depth (~8 m), the peak's height (~8.6 m, from the carport opening) and where the south face starts to rise, the courtyard behind the perforated screen, the pavilion's plan, the glazing along the gallery; the site's slope is left out."
}
